  "body": "## The report\n\nFrom a real machine:\n\n```\nerror: failed to remove directory\n  `...\\uv\\tools\\my-claude-code\\Scripts`: Access is denied. (os error 5)\n```\n\nIt left the tool environment **half-removed** — `Scripts` and `pyvenv.cfg` with no `site-packages` and no dist-info — so every shim survived while pointing at nothing:\n\n```\nmcc-server --version  →  error: uv trampoline failed to canonicalize script path\n```\n\nTwo independent defects, both Windows-only.\n\n## 1. The launcher detection drifted four features behind pyproject\n\n`Get-LauncherCommands` is a hand-maintained list that `install.ps1` checks before deciding whether to defer. It listed **18** names; pyproject publishes **26**. Missing: `mcc-desktop`, `mcc-rtk`, `mcc-help`, `mcc-anthropic-oauth-login` and their `fcc-` aliases.\n\n`mcc-desktop` is the one that bites. It's a `[project.gui-scripts]` entry, so the running app is a `pythonw.exe` executing **out of the uv tool environment**, holding that directory open. Invisible to the detection, the installer took the direct path and uv tried to delete a live environment.\n\nMeasured against the user's actually-running app:\n\n```\nOLD (published)  knows 18 names, detects running: NOTHING\nNEW (fixed)      knows 26 names, detects running: mcc-desktop\n```\n\n## 2. uv colours its output, and PowerShell's capture isn't a pipe\n\n`uv tool dir --bin` came back as `ESC[36m` + path + `ESC[39m` — **35 characters where the directory name is 25**:\n\n```\nbytes: 1b 5b 33 36 6d │ C:\\Users\\...\\.local\\bin │ 1b 5b 33 39 6d\n```\n\nSo `Test-Path` returned False for a directory that plainly exists, and the \"did this command resolve inside the tool bin?\" check could never pass.\n\nuv suppresses colour when stdout is a pipe. POSIX `$(...)` looks like one to it; **PowerShell's capture does not** — which is exactly why Linux was unaffected and this was reported as Windows-only. `Invoke-NativeCapture` now strips ANSI before returning, and `NO_COLOR` is set so uv shouldn't emit it at all. Both, because a future uv could colour some other command.\n\n## Verified in the exact failure case\n\nRan the fixed installer with the user's `mcc-desktop` live and its `pythonw.exe` holding the tool directory. It:\n\n1. **detected** the running launcher\n2. took the rename-aside hybrid path\n3. installed successfully\n4. **verified `mcc-server --version`** — which defect 2 had made impossible\n5. failed only on copying the running `mcc-desktop.exe` shim with `os error 32` — the expected, handled case that defers one shim\n\nFinal state: dist-info present, **all 13 shims present**, `my-claude-code 5.30.0` reported, install healthy.\n\n## The durable half\n\nA list that must mirror another file is a list that drifts. A contract test now compares `Get-LauncherCommands` against `[project.scripts]` + `[project.gui-scripts]` **in both directions**, and asserts the ANSI stripping is wired into `Invoke-NativeCapture`. Mutation-tested: removing `mcc-desktop` again fails it by name.\n\n## Verification\n\n**6 failed, 4354 passed, 26 skipped** vs baseline `6 failed, 4350 passed` on unmodified `fork/main` in the same shell — same six PowerShell installer failures, +4 tests, zero regressions. ruff format, ruff check, ty: clean.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- `install.sh` is **deliberately untouched**. POSIX unlinks open files, so install-while-running is native there, and Linux was confirmed unaffected.\n- The hybrid path prints both the \"staged\" notice and the \"installed and verified\" block in one run. Both are accurate — the environment installed, one shim deferred — but it reads as noisy. Pre-existing, not introduced here.\n- The six pre-existing PowerShell installer test failures are environmental (they download a real release wheel and checksum it) and are unchanged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
