    "message": "fix(installer): a running mcc-desktop no longer destroys the Windows install\n\nReported from a real machine: `uv tool install --force` failed with\n\n    error: failed to remove directory\n    `...\\uv\\tools\\my-claude-code\\Scripts`: Access is denied. (os error 5)\n\nand left the tool environment half-removed -- Scripts and pyvenv.cfg with no\nsite-packages and no dist-info -- so every shim survived while pointing at\nnothing. `mcc-server --version` answered \"uv trampoline failed to canonicalize\nscript path\".\n\nTwo independent defects, both Windows-only.\n\n1. The launcher detection had drifted four features behind pyproject.\n\n`Get-LauncherCommands` is a hand-maintained list of command names that\ninstall.ps1 checks before deciding whether to defer. It listed 18 names while\npyproject publishes 26: mcc-desktop, mcc-rtk, mcc-help and\nmcc-anthropic-oauth-login were all missing, along with their fcc- aliases.\n\nmcc-desktop is the one that bites. It is a [project.gui-scripts] entry, so the\nrunning app is a pythonw.exe executing out of the uv tool environment and\nholding that directory open. Invisible to the detection, the installer took\nthe direct path and uv tried to delete a live environment. Measured against\nthe user's running app:\n\n    OLD (published)  knows 18 names, detects running: NOTHING\n    NEW (fixed)      knows 26 names, detects running: mcc-desktop\n\n2. uv colours its output, and PowerShell's capture does not look like a pipe.\n\n`uv tool dir --bin` came back as ESC[36m + path + ESC[39m -- 35 characters\nwhere the directory name is 25:\n\n    bytes: 1b 5b 33 36 6d ... 1b 5b 33 39 6d\n\nso Test-Path returned False for a directory that plainly exists, and the\n\"did this command resolve inside the tool bin?\" check could never pass. uv\nsuppresses colour when stdout is a pipe; POSIX $(...) looks like one to it and\nPowerShell's capture does not, which is exactly why Linux was unaffected and\nthis was reported as Windows-only. Invoke-NativeCapture now strips ANSI before\nreturning, and NO_COLOR is set so uv should not emit it in the first place --\nboth, because a future uv could colour some other command.\n\nVerified by running the fixed installer in the exact failure case, with the\nuser's mcc-desktop live and its pythonw.exe holding the tool directory. It\ndetected the launcher, took the rename-aside hybrid path, installed\nsuccessfully, verified `mcc-server --version` (which the ANSI bug had made\nimpossible), and failed only on copying the running mcc-desktop.exe shim with\nos error 32 -- the expected, handled case that defers one shim to a helper.\nFinal state: dist-info present, all 13 shims present, `my-claude-code 5.30.0`\nreported, install healthy.\n\nA list that must mirror another file is a list that drifts, so the fix is not\nonly the eight names. A contract test now compares Get-LauncherCommands\nagainst [project.scripts] + [project.gui-scripts] in both directions, and\nasserts the ANSI stripping is wired into Invoke-NativeCapture. Mutation-tested:\nremoving mcc-desktop from the list again fails it by name.\n\ninstall.sh is deliberately untouched. POSIX unlinks open files, so\ninstall-while-running is native there and the user confirmed Linux is\nunaffected.\n\nVerification: full suite 6 failed, 4354 passed, 26 skipped against a baseline\nof 6 failed, 4350 passed on unmodified fork/main in the same shell -- the same\nsix PowerShell installer failures, +4 tests, zero regressions. ruff format,\nruff check, ty: clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
